WEBVTT

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.730
The Anime Club is to be shut down.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.730
Nakano-senpai, why?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.990
You screwed us over, Aurora!

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.490
Please don't call me that.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.360
I gave the club room keys 
back to the student council.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.850
I see.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.170
Sorry, this is my fault.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.850
This wouldn't have happened 
if I'd been more careful.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:08.810
No.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.730
It's not your fault, Erika-senpai.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.660
Damn it, Aurora!

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.830
I can't believe I didn't 
notice his evil conspiracy.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:16.740
I should have known.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.960
The Anime Club's gone, huh?

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.220
The school festival was such a blast, too.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.250
Yeah.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.880
Even if we lost this house, 
we would still be family.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.170
What are you talking about?

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.130
No, Dad, don't tell me you 
might get laid off again.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:39.580
Again?!

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.120
I'm making an example.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.140
Wait, so what's the point?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:48.170
Even without the container that is 
the house, a family is a family.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.120
Friends are still friends.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:54.900
Yeah.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.010
Hurry!

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:00.660
Yeah!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.160
What?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.160
<b>No shutting down
Anime Club!!</b>

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.160
<b>Don't Allow
the Principal's Tyranny!!</b>

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.160
<b>Withdraw
the Shutdown!</b>

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.950
Get out here, Principal!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.410
Don't disband the Anime Club!

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.290
What's going on?

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.420
Minoa.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.460
Over here.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.350
What exactly is going on?

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.050
I don't know, myself.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.550
We can't live without the Anime Club!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.580
To think people need us <i>this</i> much...

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.680
This is a bit extreme, though.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.680
<i>Listen up, students.</i>

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.190
It's the principal.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:35.640
<i>If you want the Anime Club's 
shutdown to be withdrawn,</i>

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>then this school is hereby closed.</i>

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.150
<i>Is this what you want?</i>

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:47.950
Yes.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.580
All it takes to silence small fry 
is to take them out of the water.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.090
<b>Principal's Office</b>

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.750
Come out, Ogikubo!

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.960
Explain this!

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.980
I can't.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.400
I've been ordered not to let anyone through.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.970
No, don't touch me!

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:11.060
If you really want to, 
you'll have to defeat me first.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.280
You'll have to push me down by force!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.870
People are enraged.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.620
I'm kind of scared.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:23.990
Move it!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.490
That's too rough!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.960
Oh, crap!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:34.830
What the...

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.430
You idiot, you just made it lock.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.090
You're all coming with 
me to the staff office.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:49.460
This is one of my feeding spots.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:54.850
What are you doing, Senpai?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.350
Don't just stand there, help me.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.070
Ow...

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.580
Principal?

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:14.180
P-Pardon me.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.080
I'm Asagaya Minoa, first-year 
student in from the Anime Club.

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.510
I heard Minoa's voice.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.130
Minoa, open up.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.840
They might not hear us from inside.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.090
Why do you hate the Anime Club so much?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.040
What the hell was that?

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:34.790
The anime short for the school festival.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.720
You broke the 180-degree rule.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.200
The artwork broke down.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.860
The lines were read monotonously.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:43.110
It was a barrage of amateurish jokes.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.950
How dare you!

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.740
I poured my soul into that art!

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:51.740
I hate to admit it, but he has a point.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.770
I actually thought so, too.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.880
Worse, you held a concert because 
you couldn't finish the ending.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.250
The title is too long!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.200
U-Uh...

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.630
Do you have anything to say for yourself?

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.050
You actually paid <i>that</i> much attention?!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.890
Thank you so much!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.810
What a passionate roast.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.660
The title is too long.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.800
The title is too long.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.730
The title is too long.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:15.390
The title is too long.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:18.460
Is the principal an anime fan?

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:22.400
Then why does he try to take the Anime 
Club down the path of destruction?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.420
Parts of it may have been bad,

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:30.410
but it's the best piece ever, 
filled with my favorite anime.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.160
Your favorite anime?

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.880
It's the anime that I saw when I was a kid.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:37.210
Robots going bam!

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.070
Grandpas going boom!

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:42.020
A girl's song defeats the enemy,

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.850
a fish goes flip flap, and an angel descends.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.420
I still have dreams about it.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.940
<i>Burndown</i>, <i>Stretch Dawn</i>,

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.580
<i>Mermaid Melody Pichipichipacchi</i>, 
and <i>Andromeda Angel</i>.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.880
All masterpieces.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.800
So how did they end up the way they did?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.060
Wow, you know so much about anime.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.920
But those aren't the anime I love.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.000
What are they called?

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.110
I don't remember.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.440
You say that with such confidence!

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.720
You're in the Anime Club, and you 
don't even remember the titles?

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.050
Is the girl from <i>Strange Midia</i>?

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.000
The giant mech, is it <i>GahXephon</i>?

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.550
Defeating an enemy with singing, 
is that <i>Super Dimension Bonsai Micross<i>?</i></i>

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:21.080
Is the angel from <i>A Dog of Decadence</i>?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:23.960
Those aren't it.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.600
The principal sure likes picking 
fights with the Anime Club.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:29.090
He's acting like a senpai.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:34.350
Come to think of it, the rough sketches in 
the club room were like <i>Midia</i> and <i>GahXephon</i>.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.970
Maybe the principal was in the Anime Club.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.220
Let's find out.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.490
A cute anime girl.

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:45.070
The raw depiction of a girl in the scene

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:48.740
where Mei Minling is given a choice 
between her life and her hair,

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.550
and she chooses her hair, was shocking.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:55.580
<i>Bishoujo Fighter Sailor Bunny</i> was the 
first shoujo battle heroine manga.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:00.790
There would never be enough time to 
talk about the heart-filled final episode.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:05.460
And man, Ham-chan in 
<i>Nurusei Yakara</i> is so devoted.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.630
I want to cheat on her so she'll zap me.

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:10.780
<i>Hiatari Sokosoko!</i> and <i>Kimamani Mikan Road</i>

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:12.380
are the two best slice-of-life 
bishoujo anime.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:16.260
Ayuyama was based on an idol that 
was really popular at the time.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.390
Holy crap, that's him!

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.830
From anime fan to anti-anime.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.510
What happened to him?

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.560
Maybe he was an aspiring 
writer who came to hate anime

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.220
after he was asked to rewrite the school 
festival script, like, 58 times.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.280
We're protecting the school 
and the Anime Club ourselves!

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.710
Pests.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:43.170
Back before the Internet, 
we read <i>Animeta</i> with hunger.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:44.710
I shall study.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.590
It's too late.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.920
Your school festival anime will 
haunt you for the rest of your life.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.060
Hey, now!

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:57.050
Making anime is hard, you know.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.440
A battle of passion and personality.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.230
Looming deadlines and dwindling stamina...

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:08.560
But it is the work of the director to bring 
the minds and talent together as one.

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:15.530
You don't get to talk 
like you're the director!

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:20.890
A director is a much more high-minded, 
noble, solitary figure.

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.160
He's by himself!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.850
Nothing gets done without the director!

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.160
Worship the director more!

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:27.540
Suck up to them!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.980
I understand.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.420
I <i>really</i> understand.

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.300
She totally doesn't.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.320
What a stuffy talk, though.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:39.810
Do you think the principal 
was an anime director?

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.710
It's possible.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.810
Aurora!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.180
Why are you here?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:46.560
I'm sorry!

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.270
There's a reason for this.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.690
We don't need your excuses, Aurora-senpai.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.940
It's too late, Aurora-senpai.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.820
I have five siblings.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:58.950
Six Aurora-senpais?!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.700
My older brothers are all 
complete losers, and...

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.700
Wait, let's not talk about this.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:08.210
Anyway, I worked my butt off 
at a high-class coffee shop.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.640
The principal was a regular there.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.560
With my family's financial problems, 
I wasn't sure I should attend high school.

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.220
That's when he gave me a hand.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.770
That's why I can't go against what he says.

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.340
It was so terrible.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:25.820
Aurora-senpai, I had no idea.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:28.050
Yet you were always smiling.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:31.180
Aurora, damn it, man!

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:32.390
Bliss!

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:34.480
I can't blame you, then.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:36.860
Welcome back, Auroracchi.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.390
Thanks, everyone.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:45.230
Also, can you stop calling me Aurora?

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.870
The director is number one!

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:49.410
Of course!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.270
After talking to you, I'm as pumped 
as ever to get back to work.

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:54.280
Back to work?

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:56.130
I'll work even harder on the second piece.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.260
Second piece?

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.880
Because I love anime.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.480
Even without the Anime Club, we're friends.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.640
As long as we're together, 
we can make a second one.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:11.650
There is no second one.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.340
Everything's over if you 
screw up the first episode.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:22.790
Even if you devote your entire 
being into creating two seasons,

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:26.290
if the first episode gets 
canceled, it's all over.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.790
What's going on?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.530
It's not my fault!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.040
It's not my fault!

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.090
It's the anime fans' fault!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:42.350
Every freaking night, they gather in the 
corners of the Internet, nitpicking.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.800
Who the hell is "anon" anyway? Damn it all!

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:49.560
Have you made anime before, Principal?

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.540
So he <i>was</i> a director.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.440
But canned after the first episode?

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.950
He got dissed too hard; it broke him.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:59.940
As a creator, I have nothing but sympathy.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:04.250
My work was banished into oblivion!

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:05.820
What a pain.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.390
Neko-chan.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:09.480
It's Neko-senpai!

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.380
Cold!

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:12.520
There's a cat door here.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:14.830
He's surprisingly fond of cats.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.430
Minoa, are you all right?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.070
Arisu-chan?

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.400
Open up.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.340
Uh...

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:26.740
There are a ton of buttons.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.340
I don't know.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.720
Principal, what's the password?

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.910
He can't hear your voices right now.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.860
The lock to the door is the 
lock to his heart, perhaps.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.410
Lock to his heart?

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:45.110
He probably means that until the principal 
opens his heart, it will never open.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.300
What are you, chuuni?

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.620
You're one to talk.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:50.740
A password that would open his heart?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:56.750
If he broke down because of anime, 
he can only be saved through anime.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:57.800
Indeed.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.090
A ray of light at the end of the darkness.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.800
Let's find it!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:02.510
Yeah.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.950
Begin Project M.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.640
Ambitious start!

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.320
Minoa, I promise I'll find 
the principal's anime.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.390
And I'll save you.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.060
A-As soon as possible, please.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:27.030
<b>Anime Club Finally Falls</b>

00:13:32.780 --> 00:13:34.540
Let's just gather information.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.440
I'll go talk to people who might know.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:43.420
I'm counting on you.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.920
Principal Canceled Password

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.900
I'm not getting any hits.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.930
We'll have to crowdsource this.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.240
Hello? Saori-san?

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.810
I want to ask you something.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:57.670
Live streaming is an option, too.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:05.940
To anime fans all across the world, 
my name is Kamiigusa Arisu.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.200
I'm looking for an anime.

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:12.700
